Sometimes you need to stop a path before it finishes — for example, when a color sensor detects a game element.

Instead of letting the path run to completion, add a condition to the command:

FollowPathCommand cmd = new FollowPathCommand(follower, chain);
cmd.interruptOn(() -> colorSensor.red() > 100);
schedule(cmd);

When the condition returns true, the path stops immediately and the Follower holds position. This is how teams react to sensor input mid-path without writing complex state machines.
